kien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T08:40:58Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T08:40:58Z","body":"> [#113497 (comment)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113497#issuecomment-3613286742) is a good example of why this does not work in practice and probably a waste of both parties' time for repeated bisections.\r\n> \r\n> It's perfectly normal for people to overlook large blocks of text.\r\n\r\nOne person overlooking information doesn't mean that the information is useless. I didn't overlook it myself and if I were to bisect I would have started from dev5, as identified by you as the last `good` version.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3615837033/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3615844127","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113405#issuecomment-3615844127","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113405","id":3615844127,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XhWcf","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T08:43:25Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T08:44:25Z","body":"On the other hand I agree that we shouldn't necessarily get people to test like 10 versions and report the status for each of them. What's useful, especially for regressions, is to know what is the last version which doesn't show the bug, and the first version which shows it.\r\n\r\nSo in practice a good report for a regression that happened in say 4.6-dev5 should be something like:\r\n- Reproducible in 4.6-dev5\r\n- Not reproducible in 4.5.1-stable or 4.6-dev4\r\n\r\nIn most cases, it wouldn't be useful to also get 4.5-stable, 4.4-stable, 4.6-dev1, etc. listed. If users want to list more it's fine, but the focus should be on identifying when things broke.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3615844127/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3615850635","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113405#issuecomment-3615850635","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113405","id":3615850635,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XhYCL","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T08:45:31Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T08:57:26Z","body":"Indeed I'll adjust the description to emphasizing that, and might move it to the placeholder, and try to emphasize that there's no pressure to test many versions but that the more information we have the better\r\n\r\nAlso to emphasize the actual meaning of the text, but might need improvements to avoid misunderstanding: this does *not* demand people test things more, obviously, this just asks people to describe what they already know when making the report \r\n\r\nBut I have several times run into issues where the author didn't add the information they already had and added only later, and it adds unnecessary delay or causes unnecessary work in cases where, for example, I would have to test versions myself ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3615850635/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3615877619","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113405#issuecomment-3615877619","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113405","id":3615877619,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Xhenz","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T08:54:01Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T08:54:01Z","body":"Will look at reworking the whole block and leveraging the placeholder, perhaps add an example of how to report a bisected regression as well","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3615877619/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3615894469","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113405#issuecomment-3615894469","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113405","id":3615894469,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XhivF","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T09:00:56Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T09:02:38Z","body":"In general I do agree that big blocks of text in the issue template tend to be overlooked, which is why I haven't been too fond of the gradual increase of the text-heaviness of our template (though I fully understand why it was done and this information is needed).\r\n\r\nI think we should aim at moving most of the details to a dedicated docs page (which I know @AThousandShips already started working on) and then significantly reduce the text in the template itself, replacing with the absolute necessary + links to the docs page.\r\n\r\nTo be clear I'm not proposing to change the actual fields of the template, or what we expect users to write in them, but just the contextual descriptions (intro, and then on each field) which IMO lead many users to just TL;DR.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"867\" height=\"760\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5fe7454-a38a-430d-b2ea-1d8a8ebfc28b\" />\r\n\r\nWith shorter description we should be able to increase the likelihood that users do read them (and so they should focus on the most important point(s)), and the docs page should be linked prominently in `CONTRIBUTING.md`, in the template, and referenced in saved replies when asking reporters to backfill more information.\r\n\r\nAnd indeed leveraging the placeholder text can help give users a quick understanding of what's expected without having to read a whole block of text. But there are a couple things to be aware of:\r\n- It shouldn't itself become a big block of text that users might overlook.\r\n- Starting to type anything will hide the placeholder so it can't be referred back if it included information that needs a bit of time/practice to internalize.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3615894469/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3615906247","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113405#issuecomment-3615906247","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113405","id":3615906247,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XhlnH","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscripti